000200 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000300 PROGRAM-ID.          TIRWSOK.
000400 AUTHOR.              C HILLES.
000500 DATE-WRITTEN.        9/15/83.
000600 DATE-COMPILED.
000700*INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
000800*SECURITY.
000900*REMARKS.     ISSUE AND RETURN WORKSHEET MODIFY PROGRAM.
001000*
001100*    ON NOVEMBER 4, 1983, CHANGED THE PROGRAM TO PRINT THE
001200*    ITEMS CLOSER TOGETHER ON PAGE (FOR UC - THEY LINE THE
001300*    PERF UP WITH THE PLASTIC TOP OF PRINTER TO BE ABLE TO
001400*    TEAR IT OFF WITHOUT FORM FEED).  ALSO ADDED A
001500*    "NOW EDITING" MESSAGE BEFORE "NOW PROCESSING" MSG.
001600*    CIH.
001700*
001800*    ON NOVEMBER 15, 1983, CHANGED THE PRINT ROUTINE FOR
001900*    HALF-SIZE SHEETS (5.5 INCHES).  ALTHOUGH WILL STILL WORK
002000*    FOR FULL SHEETS, WORKS BETTER WITH THE 5.5 IN.  SWITCHES
002100*    ON THE PRINTER MUST NOW BE SET SO THAT FORM LENGTH IS 5.5 IN
002200*    IN EITHER CASE.  NOW FORM FEEDS AFTER EACH ITEM AND THEN
002300*    DOUBLE FORM FEED AT THE END.  FOR NOW THIS IS
002400*    FOR GADSDEN AND DANVILLE ONLY (THESE ARE THE ONES
002500*    WITH 5.5 PAPER).  CIH.
002600*
002700*    ADDED LAWTON TO THE HALF-SHEET PLANTS.  CIH.
002800*
002900*    ON NOVEMBER 21, 1983, CHANGED TO WORK FOR EITHER HALF-SHEET
003000*    PLANTS OF FULL-SHEET PLANTS.  ADDED THE ESC &l6V ESCAPE
003100*    SEQUENCE BACK IN TO ADVANCE A HALF-PAGE AFTER ODD ITEMS.
003200*    CIH.
003300*
003400*    ON NOVEMBER 30, 1983, CHANGED PARAMETERS FOR CALL TO
003500*    "TSPLPRT".  NOW RETURNS ENTIRE SPOOLER REC, BUT NO
003600*    MESSAGE BUFFER.  CIH.
003700*
003800*    ON FEBRUARY 10, 1984, CHANGED PARAMETERS FOR CALL TO
003900*    "TREQFILU".  THE FIELDS "STR-RESERVED" AND "
004000*    "SAVE-RSRVD-BEFORE" WERE ADDED.  THIS IS BECAUSE THE
004100*    REQFILE UPDATE SUBPROGRAM WILL NOW CREATE AUTO REQS ON THE
004200*    BASIS OF AVAILABLE RATHER THAN ONHAND.  CIH.
004300*
004400*    ON APRIL 24, 1984, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
004500*       1.  ADDED A "NO-PRINT" OPTION TO THE PROCESS WORKSHEET.
004600*           THE USER MAY SPECIFY ON THE SCREEN WHETHER HE WISHES
004700*           TO PRINT THE WITHDRAWAL DOCUMENTS OR NOT.  IF NOT,
004800*           NOTHING WILL BE PRINTED AND THE WORKSHEET WILL BE
004900*           USED AS THE WITHDRAWAL DOCUMENT.  (THE WORKSHEET
005000*           HAS ADDED TO IT A SPACE FOR EMPLOYEE SIGNATURE).
005100*       2.  THE 5TH SPOOL NUMBER FROM SPOOLER REC WAS USED AS
005200*           KEY AS TO WHETHER HALF-SHEET PAPER IS USED (AND
005300*           THERFORE WHETHER TO ADVANCE TWICE AFTER PRINTING
005400*           OR NOT).  HOWEVER THIS KEY WAS NOT RETURNED TO MAIN
005500*           PROGRAM.  THUS WHENEVER A USER EXITED FROM A SUB-
005600*           PROGRAM THE PRINT CEASED TO FORM-FEED PROPERLY.
005700*           THIS PROBLEM IS FIXED BY PASSING THE ENTIRE SPOOLER-
005800*           REC (USER, ACCOUNT, ALL 5 SPOOL NUMBERS, ETC) BETWEEN
005900*           THE SUBPROGRAMS.
006000*    3.  CHANGED THE "DWLITEM-LIST" (DATA ITEM LIST
006100*    FOR DWLITEM SEGMENT) TO "ALL-ITEMS" (PULL OUT ALL ITEMS
006200*    IN DATA SET).  THIS IS BECAUSE THE TEST DATABASE HAD A
006300*    DATA ITEM CHANGED IN DWLITEM, BUT IT WAS NOT CHANGED AT ALL
006400*    PLANTS (YET).  CIH.
006500*
006600*    ON AUGUST 10, 1984, CHANGED THE "DDAILY-TC-LIST" TO
006700*    "ALL-ITEMS", BECAUSE WE CHANGED THE DATA ITEMS IN THE
006800*    DDAILYTC DATA-SET, AND ALL PLANTS DO NOT YET HAVE THE
006900*    CHANGE.  CIH.
007000*
007100*    ON SEPT 10, 1984, MADE THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
007200*      1.  ADDED A "BASE" PARAMETER FOR THE CALL TO "TREQFILU".
007300*          THIS IS BECAUSE THE KSAM FILE "REQFILE" IS GOING
007400*          TO BE ELIMINATED AND THE DATA PUT IN A NEW DATA
007500*          SEGMENT IN THE STORES DATABASE.  THE REQFILE FILE
007600*          NUMBER PARAMETER IS LEFT IN THE CALL SO THAT PROGRAMS
007700*          WILL WORK ON EITHER THE KSAM REQFILE OR THE DATABASE
007800*          REQFILE (SINCE "TREQFILU" IS IN THE ACCOUNT SL, NO
007900*          DIFFERENT VERSIONS OF PROGRAMS WILL HAVE TO BE
008000*          MAINTAINED FOR PLANTS THAT HAVE NOT YET MADE THE
008100*          DATABASE CHANGE).
008200*
008300*      2.  TOOK OUT THE OPEN OF THE KSAM FILE "REQFILE", AND ALL
008400*          THE KSAM WORK AREAS.  FROM NOW ON, THE OLD VERSION
008500*          OF "TREQFILU" (KSAM VERSION) WILL OPEN THE REQFILE
008600*          IF THE PASSED FILE NUMBER IS 0, THEN WILL RETURN THE
008700*          FILE NUMBER OF THE OPENED FILE.  THIS WAY THE FILE
008800*          WILL BE OPENED ONLY ONCE.  (THERE WILL BE NO FORMAL
008900*          CLOSE OF THE REQFILE).  FOR THE NEW VERSION OF
009000*          "TREQFILU" (DATABASE VERSION), OF COURSE NO KSAM
009100*          OPEN WILL BE NEEDED (AND THE REQFILE FILE NUMBER
009200*          PASSED WILL BE IGNORED).
009300*
009400*    ON OCT 8, 1984, CHANGED THIS SUBPROGRAM TO WORK FOR BOTH
009500*    THE AKRON PLANTS AND THE SUB-PLANTS.  FORMERLY THERE WAS
009600*    A SEPERATE VERSION OF ALL THE STORES PROGRAMS FOR AKRON
009700*    PLANTS.  THIS INVOLVED THE FOLLOWING CHANGES:
009800*        1.  THE "DEFAULT EXPENSE CLASS" LOGIC WAS MOVED FROM
009900*            THIS SUBPROGRAM INTO THE "TIREDIT" EDITING SUB-
010000*            PROGRAM.  THIS REQUIRED ADDING THE "STR-EXP-CLASS"
010100*            AS A PARAMETER TO THE CALL OF "TIREDIT".
010200*            (DEFAULT EXP CLASS IS NOT USED IN AKRON, AND THE
010300*            EDITING SUB-PROGRAM WILL HANDLE THESE DIFFERENCES).
010400*
010500*        2.  AN "IF AKRON" STATEMENT WAS ADDED FOR UPDATING OF
010600*            LAST CHARGE DEPT.  THE STORES PROGRAMS ARE USED
010700*            FOR Z, IT, J BILLS, MATERIAL TRANSFERS, AND SPECIAL
010800*            STORES ISSUES.  IN THESE CASES, DIFFERENT FIELDS
010900*            MAY UPDATE "STR-LAST-CHARGE" OTHER THAN THE CHARGE
011000*            DEPT FIELD.  HOPEFULLY, SOON THESE FUNCTIONS WILL
011100*            BE MOVED OUT OF THE STORES PROGRAMS TO A SEPERATE
011200*            PROGRAM (WHERE THEY SHOULD BE).  AT THIS TIME THIS
011300*            LOGIC WILL BE REMOVED.
011400*
011500*        3.  THE "TIREDIT", "TQTYEDIT", "TWSPRT" SUBPROGRAMS WERE
011600*            CHANGED WITH SPECIAL LOGIC FOR AKRON.
011700*
011800*        4.  IN THE PRINT ROUTINE, IF AKRON A "CENTER" HEADING
011900*            IS ADDED FOR THE WORK CENTER FIELD.
012000*
012100*        5.  A DIFFERENT FORMS FILE IS MAINTAINED FOR AKRON AND THE
012200*            PLANTS.  THE AKRON VERSION HAS A "WORK CENTER" FIELD.
012300*            THE PLANT VERSION HAS THIS FIELD, BUT IT IS DISPLAY
012400*            ONLY, NO ENHANCEMENTS (INVISIBLE).  (THUS THE SCREEN
012500*            BUFFER IS THE SAME IN THE PROGRAM).  THE AKRON VERSION
012600*            HAS A 1 BYTE "CHARGE TYPE FIELD".  THE PLANTS VERSION
012700*            HAS A 2 BYTE EXTENSION TO THE CHARGE DEPT.  SO ON
012800*            THE AKRON FORM FILE, THE SECOND HALF THE THIS EXTENSION
012900*            FIELD WAS CHANGED TO  DISPLAY ONLY, NO ENHANCEMENTS.
013000*            (ONCE AGAIN, SO THAT THE SCREEN BUFFER DOES NOT NEED
013100*            TO BE DIFFERENT FOR THE TWO VERSIONS).
013200*             CIH.
013300*
013400**   ON MAY 16, 1985, CHANGED THIS SUBPROGRAM FOR THE
013500*    EUROPEAN DATE CONVERSION.  IT WILL NOW CALL "TDATECHK"
013600*    FOR ALL DATE MANIPULATION, WHICH WILL RESULT IN A
013700*    EUROPEAN STLYE DATE ON THE OUTPUT DOCUMENT IF THE
013800*    EUROPEAN DATE FLAG IS SET.  CIH.
013900*
014000*    ON JULY 25, 1985, CHANGED THIS SUBPROGRAM TO DISALLOW
014100*    PROCESSING OF FROZEN CODES.  IF A CODE IS IN THE FROZEN
014200*    STATE ON A PARTICULAR WORKSHEET  THE USER WILL NOT BE
014300*    ABLE TO PROCESS THAT WORKSHEET.  DEH.
014400*
014500*   10/09/85  ADDED CALLS TO FINDJCW, NLAPPEND, CATOPEN, AND
014600*             CATCLOSE IN ORDER TO ACCOMODATE THE NATIVE
014700*             LANGUAGE SUPPORT FACILITY.  ADDED LINKAGES AND
014800*             ALSO MADE THE CHANGE TO THE FORMFILE NAMES.
014900*   10/09/85  CHANGED ALL REFERENCES OF TSCRPRNT TO TSCRPRT2,
015000*             TDATECHK TO TDATECK2.
015100*             THIS WAS TO INCORPORATE THE NATIVE LANGUAGE
015200*             SUPPORT VERSIONS OF THESE SUBROUTINES.
015300*                               -TW COTTON.
015400*
015500*    03/03/86.
015600*      CHANGED PROGRAM TO MOVE THE PRINT OPTION FOR WORKSHEETS
015700*      TO THE 30TH BYTE OF "SPOOLER REC" - SO IT WILL BE
015800*      RETURNED TO CALLING PROGRAM AND SAVED.  THEN A PUTBUFFER
015900*      IS DONE EACH TIME THIS PROGRAM IS CALLED.  THIS IS SO
016000*      WHICHEVER PRINT OPTION THEY PICK IS NOT LOST WHEN GETTING
016100*      OUT OF THE PROGRAM.  CIH.
016200*
016300*    06/17/86.
016400*      REPLACED CALL TO "TFDESC" WITH CALL TO "CDESC".  "CDESC"
016500*      HAS MORE OPTIONS, AND HANDLES THE DATA SETS "DMANPART" - USING
016600*      THE MANUFACTURER ENTRIES AS PART OF DESCRIPTION. CIH.
016700*
016800*      JUNE 27, 1986                C.R. KALMAN
016900*         1. HARD-CODED ESCAPE SEQUENCES REMOVED FROM
017000*            PROGRAM.  THEY ARE NOW TO BE EXTERNALLY
017100*            SUPPLIED.
017200*         2. THE MAIN PROGRAM IN A JOB STREAM WILL
017300*            COPY ESC-NAM2 THAT CONTAINS THE HP
017400*            ESCAPE SEQUENCES.  IT WILL ALSO CALL
017500*            TESCSEQ THAT CONTAINS THE NON-HP ESCAPE
017600*            SEQUENCES, IF ANY ARE USED.  THE NON-HP
017700*            SEQUENCES WILL OVERRIDE THE HP SEQUENCES.
017800*         3. THE ACTUAL PRINTING PROGRAM WILL GET THE
017900*            APPROPRIATE SEQUENCES PASSED DOWN TO IT
018000*            THRU THE INTERMEDIATE SUBROUTINES THAT
018100*            COPY ESC-NAME.
      *C
      *C   02NOV1994    WILL MCINTYRE   REQUEST 94-027
      *C     ADDED NEW PARMS TO CALL TQTYEDIT.  HOWEVER WILL BYPASS
      *C     CHECKS ON RETURN LIMITS.
018200*C
      *C   MAY 31, 1995  JEFF BUNGO     REQUEST #94-058
      *C     ADDED PARAMETERS TO CALL OF TQTYEDIT TO WRITE TO MSTRWITH
      *C     IN CASE WITHDRAWAL HAS INSUFFICIENT ON HAND.
      *C
      *C   06/12/96  JEFF BUNGO
      *C     EXPAND DATE FIELDS FOR YEAR 2000 COMPLIANCE.
      *C     INCLUDE CENTURY FOR ACTIVITY AND LAST ISSUE DATES.
      *C
      *C   06/13/96  JEFF BUNGO
      *C     REMOVE COMPRESSED PRINTING FROM THE HEADINGS.
      *C
      *C   05/07/97  JEFF BUNGO
      *C     PASS NEW PARAMETERS CODE OWNER, BIN OWNER, AND
      *C     FRANCHISE TABLE TO TQTYEDIT.  RETRIEVE FRAN TABLE
      *C     FROM MPLTINFO.  FOR EACH OWNER WITHDRAWN FROM
      *C     CREATE A SEPARATE TC.
      *C
      *C   09/17/97  JEFF BUNGO
      *C     AKRON RESEARCH (119) ONLY.
      *C     AFTER A WORKSHEET HAS BEEN PROCESSED, CHECK IF ANY
      *C     CCS DATA HAD BEEN ENTERED FOR THE WORKSHEET.  IF
      *C     FOUND, UPDATE THE RECORDS WITH THE PROCESSED DATE
      *C     AND TIME.  THIS IS THE INDICATION TO SEND THE RECORDS
      *C     TO THE CCS SYSTEM.
018300*C
      *C   OCTOBER 1995  JIM COFFMAN
      *C     CHANGED ISSPARTS PARAMETERS TO BE INCLUDED IN A COPYLIB
      *C     MEMBER. THIS WAS NECESSARY TO ALLOW THE AREA TO BE
      *C     EXPANDABLE TO CONTAIN THE LINK TO A WORK ORDER LOGIC
      *C     REQUEST NOW AVAILABLE IN AN E1 REQUISITION CREATE.
      *C
      *C   SEPT 22, 1998  CA YODER
      *C     ADDED CALL TO MCXSNDMSG TO SEND A MESSAGE TO USERS
      *C     SPECIFIED IN MCFPCSUSER FILE WHEN A PARTICULAR CODE
      *C     IS WITHDRAWN FROM THE STOREROOM.
      *C
018400 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
018500 CONFIGURATION SECTION.
018600 SOURCE-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
018700 OBJECT-COMPUTER.  HP-3000.
018800 COPY SPECIALN IN COPYLIB.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT ONLINE-PRT ASSIGN TO PRINTER-MCPRT.
           SELECT MSTORERM-CD-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0201
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DWLITEM-WK-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1501
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MWRKLIST-WK-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0301
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DCCSDATA
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS6601
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                    WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT MPLTINFO
               ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS0501
               ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                 ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
               FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DDAILYTC-DT-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCS1601
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT USER-I
               ASSIGN         TO DATABASE-MCFLCSUSER
               ORGANIZATION   IS INDEXED
               ACCESS MODE    IS DYNAMIC
               RECORD KEY     IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                              WITH DUPLICATES
               FILE STATUS    IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DISPLAY-FILE
                  ASSIGN TO WORKSTATION-ZUDCSTR-SI
                  ORGANIZATION IS TRANSACTION
                  ACCESS IS SEQUENTIAL
                  FILE STATUS IS DISPLAY-STATUS
                  CONTROL-AREA IS WS-CONTROL.

